---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, legal } from '@config/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Evidence Axis handles the limited information you share through the inquiry form and business correspondence."
  path="/privacy/"
  noindex={false}
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy" meta={[`Last updated ${legal.lastUpdated}`]} />

  <section class="section container">
    <div class="legal measure">
      <p class="legal__intro">
        This note explains, in practical terms, what information {site.name} collects through this
        website and how it is used. It covers the website only. Any engagement is governed by the
        terms agreed for that specific project.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        If you submit the inquiry form, we receive the details you choose to enter — typically your
        name, work email, company, role, the decision or research question, the competitors you want
        investigated, and any context you add. We use this only to understand, scope and respond to
        your inquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>Business correspondence</h2>
      <p>
        If we correspond about a possible or active engagement, we keep the information reasonably
        needed to carry out and account for that work. We do not sell it, and we do not use it for
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Technical information</h2>
      <p>
        Basic technical information (such as standard server request data) may be processed to keep
        the site available and secure. Where analytics or cookies are introduced, this note will be
        updated to describe them specifically, and any consent required will be requested at that
        point. The site does not set advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Where we engage third-party providers to operate the site or deliver a brief — for example,
        website hosting or receiving inquiry submissions — they would process information only on our
        instructions. No such providers should be assumed to be in place until they have been
        selected, and this note will name any material processors once they are.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep inquiry and engagement information for as long as reasonably necessary for the
        purpose it was provided, and for legitimate business and record-keeping needs, then remove
        it. If you would like your inquiry information removed, contact us through the inquiry form
        and we will address it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what inquiry information we hold about you and request that it be corrected or
        removed. Depending on your location, additional rights may apply; we will honor applicable
        requirements. Reaching us through the inquiry form is the fastest route.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this note can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">inquiry form</a>. As
        the practice's contracting entity and formal contact details are finalized ahead of launch,
        this page will be updated to reflect them.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__foot mono">
        This is a practical website privacy note, not a substitute for advice on your own
        obligations. It will be reviewed and expanded before public launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__intro { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--text); }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-top: var(--space-s); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .legal p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-s); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal__foot { margin-top: var(--space-xl); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--text-faint); }
</style>
